  "endpoint": {
    "family_id": "T12",
    "http_method": "POST",
    "route": "add_attachment_to_plan_entry/{plan_id}/{entry_id}",
    "tool": "testrail_add_attachment_to_plan_entry",
    "driver_method": "attachments.addAttachmentToPlanEntry"
  },
  "sources": [
    {
      "id": "driver-module",
      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/src/modules/attachments.ts",
      "supports": "addAttachmentToPlanEntry validates the plan ID and the entry ID, places them in that order after add_attachment_to_plan_entry and posts the file through the shared multipart pipeline with the caller's filename under the none retry policy, parsing no schema. Its comment records that entry_id is the plan entry's GUID and that TestRail refuses a numeric one with 400."
    },
    {
      "id": "driver-validation",
      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/src/validation.ts",
      "supports": "validateId accepts any positive integer: it tests Number.isInteger and has no safe-integer bound, so the largest-safe-integer ceiling on these identifiers is this server's own. validateEntryId and validateAttachmentId test strings against one case-insensitive UUID expression anchored at both ends, so a traversal sequence, a surrounding space or a trailing line terminator is refused; validateAttachmentId otherwise accepts any positive integer, with the same missing bound."
    },
    {
      "id": "driver-client",
      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/src/client-core.ts",
      "supports": "The multipart pipeline appends the file to a FormData under the field name attachment with the caller's filename, and opens the staged path as a blob whose media type is the one supplied, as given, or empty when none was; FormData lowercases it when it wraps the blob as a File. That form data is the request body, sent without a JSON content type. The upload methods name the none retry policy, which re-sends nothing, not even a 429; retry-policy.ts gives the reason as an upload not being idempotent and TestRail documenting no retry semantics for creating an attachment."
    },
    {
      "id": "driver-constants",
      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/src/constants.ts",
      "supports": "MULTIPART_FIELD_NAME is attachment."
    },
    {
      "id": "driver-retry",
      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/src/retry-policy.ts",
      "supports": "NO_RETRY_POLICY, the none policy, retries no status and no network error. It is used by multipart uploads, which are not idempotent and for which TestRail documents no retry semantics, so zero retries is the safe default."
    },
    {
      "id": "driver-cli",
      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/src/cli/file-input.ts",
      "supports": "The filename flag overrides the basename-derived filename when a caller wants to rename on upload, and callers reading from stdin are encouraged to pass one so TestRail stores a sensible value."
    },
    {
      "id": "driver-skill",
      "url": "https://github.com/dichovsky/testrail-api-client/blob/cc7751c01c3d3956d061073283bee6b23bf33422/skill/SKILL.md",
      "supports": "The --filename option overrides the path basename so the attachment shows up with a meaningful name in the TestRail UI."
    },
    {
      "id": "testrail-attachments",
      "url": "https://support.testrail.com/hc/en-us/articles/7077196481428-Attachments",
      "supports": "add_attachment_to_plan_entry/{plan_id}/{entry_id} requires TestRail 6.3 or later; its description, copied from the plan section, says it adds an attachment to a test plan. Both IDs are labelled integer. The upload must be multipart/form-data, the maximum upload size is 256MB, and the reply is {\"attachment_id\": 443}. It answers 400 for a malformed request or invalid ID parameters and 403 for no access or insufficient permissions."
    },
    {
      "id": "testrail-accessing",
      "url": "https://support.testrail.com/hc/en-us/articles/7077039051284-Accessing-the-TestRail-API",
      "supports": "The documented attachment upload posts the file as the multipart field attachment to add_attachment_to_result/1 and receives {\"attachment_id\":11}."
    }
  ],
  "input_policy": {
    "ordinary_fields": "reject",
    "custom_fields": "reject",
    "notes": "Strictness is an MCP boundary requirement. The transport requires the caller's file to lie within the configured upload roots, stages an owned copy of it in its own staging directory before dispatch and hands the driver that copy, so the bytes sent are the bytes approved; the containment, the staging, its size limit and its disposal belong to the transport rather than to this endpoint."
  },
  "outer_result": {
    "driver": "record",
    "tool_data": "record",
    "notes": "TestRail answers with the new attachment_id, returned as the driver received it: the upload methods parse no schema. Drift is checked, advisorily, against the driver's attachment schema with attachment_id required as a number, since the reference documents it as always included."
  },
